:"59117e6f-0ad2-4866-ac9e-5c455ecb89e5-attachment.png","ext":".png","contentType":"image/png","contentLength":243536,"name":"newspec-c/evidence/tc06-s21-s22-iphone15-hospital-chart-preround.png"},"type":"attachment"},{"link":{"used":true,"missed":false,"id":"f6bed9aa654e3c680b005264e55c6c94","originalFileName":"957d21db-60d1-4c4d-af9a-3830326e2740-attachment.json","ext":".json","contentType":"application/json","contentLength":1917,"name":"newspec-c/evidence/tc06-s21-s22-iphone15-nh-add.json"},"type":"attachment"},{"link":{"used":true,"missed":false,"id":"eb4d4f0de60f28269c6e56d47bada515","originalFileName":"dbf612e7-f421-4400-9383-74e96172286d-attachment.png","ext":".png","contentType":"image/png","contentLength":184341,"name":"newspec-c/evidence/tc06-s21-s22-iphone15-nh-add.png"},"type":"attachment"},{"link":{"used":true,"missed":false,"id":"5597af59f089045c8dd6daa5296110d9","originalFileName":"0773adc2-1019-42d2-b73f-f24b564d623f-attachment.json","ext":".json","contentType":"application/json","contentLength":2031,"name":"newspec-c/evidence/tc06-s21-s22-iphone15-nh-chart-encounter.json"},"type":"attachment"},{"link":{"used":true,"missed":false,"id":"171724c9ac7adc691d3a3ca7b0380bb0","originalFileName":"e2480d6d-d7d8-4056-a497-a05590c7a01d-attachment.png","ext":".png","contentType":"image/png","contentLength":169811,"name":"newspec-c/evidence/tc06-s21-s22-iphone15-nh-chart-encounter.png"},"type":"attachment"},{"link":{"used":true,"missed":false,"id":"12540e7e356a785e70d3e6e795fb4a91","originalFileName":"0a479153-95b7-4fdf-85fd-f5afe307d5b2-attachment.json","ext":".json","contentType":"application/json","contentLength":4166,"name":"newspec-c/evidence/tc06-s21-s22-iphone15-nh-chart-preround.json"},"type":"attachment"},{"link":{"used":true,"missed":false,"id":"d00273b400b5741596c0988aed8c07c4","originalFileName":"7ea72c15-da5d-4805-b4be-ad082ac2dba5-attachment.png","ext":".png","contentType":"image/png","contentLength":219343,"name":"newspec-c/evidence/tc06-s21-s22-iphone15-nh-chart-preround.png"},"type":"attachment"},{"link":{"id":"6bb5d6b8cb1d994bb157e9863fee09d0","originalFileName":"ed42201b-fc2a-4f88-a0b3-02fe0c692bad-attachment.json","ext":".json","name":"newspec-c/evidence/tc06-s21-s22-iphone15.json","contentType":"application/json","used":true,"missed":false,"contentLength":29865},"type":"attachment"},{"link":{"used":true,"missed":false,"id":"7750854a1ddb666ee6d52bb1d10ee76f","originalFileName":"c421d425-5161-4f8c-ae31-77369ffe42e3-attachment.json","ext":".json","contentType":"application/json","contentLength":3844,"name":"lane result (newspec-c/results.json)"},"type":"attachment"}],"error":{"message":"newspec-c: record-only → passed (record only (every judged cell passed, the rest is recorded only))\nOur own addition: record-only, findings are suggestions. Same run as S21 (Pixel 7 Chromium 412 px, iPhone 15 WebKit 393 px, plus desktop). The transparent status select was measured directly (the visual lane skips opacity-0 elements): it fills its outer <label> exactly, 88x20 CSS px, on all four chart screens and all three profiles. 20 px is below the 24 px of WCAG 2.5.8 but passes its spacing exception (the nearest other target is 99 px from the control's centre on the Hospital chart, 33 px on the Nursing Home chart); it is below the ideal 44 pt (suggestion). The topmost element at the badge's centre is the select itself (a tap reaches it, nothing covers it); the badge text 'Follow-up ▾' is not clipped and the badge sits inside the screen on both phones; no covered / overflow / truncated finding of medium or high severity on any of the six screens. The add forms' Encounter Type control is visible without sideways scroll on both phones (page width = viewport); on Pixel 7 it is 37 px tall, on iPhone 15 WebKit 22 px tall (< 24 px, WebKit's native select height), and the Note Format picker is also 22 px tall on WebKit (41 px on Chromium) - suggestions for a real-device look."},"testCase":{"id":"88e5f9dd645921f0a23ee4d63d6a3a9a","externalId":"966775ba16d497fc2042af0ef53c6ccc","name":"[local] S22 Badge control on phone widths and WebKit: tappable, not covered or clipped","fullName":"TC-06 Admission Status Toggle › TC-06/S22"},"descriptionHtml":"<div class=\"rc-approach\"><p><b>Approach</b> · TC-06 Admission Status Toggle · <b>S22</b> Badge control on phone widths and WebKit: tappable, not covered or clipped</p><p><b>UAT steps / ticket ACs covered:</b></p><ul><li><b>U4</b> The physician can change the badge by hand at any time (before or after Generate, and on a patient whose status already rolled) through all three states, and each change persists (list, chart, reload … (UAT TC-06; TFA-92584 AC 1)</li><li><b>U3</b> The manual add form has the three-state toggle (New Admission / Follow-up / Consult) at creation, it defaults to Follow-up, and the state chosen there (or left untouched) is the one saved (UAT TC-06; TFA-92584 AC 2; TFA-92584 AC 3)</li></ul><p><b>Test design technique: </b>Device (device) — Look at the layout and gestures at phone size or on a real device (iPhone / Pixel).</p><p><b>Given </b>Visual lane profiles Pixel 7 (Chromium) and iPhone 15 (WebKit)</p><p><b>When </b>Load the chart header and add-form screens</p><p><b>Then </b>The Admission status control is at least 24 px (WCAG 2.5.8) and ideally 44 pt; badge text is not covered or truncated; the add-form toggle is visible without sideways scroll</p><p><b>Pass rule (oracle, excerpt): </b>visual-checks.ts tap / covered / truncated / overflow findings on the status select (it matches the select element); findings are evidence for a human</p><p><b>Where it ran: </b>local newspec-c (new Playwright specs); test method VISUAL · Visual (screenshots for a person); lane planned in the matrix: visual / mobile (automated)</p><p><small>S22 is our own case number (its number in the coverage matrix cases/TC-06.matrix.json), not a step number of the UAT document.</small></p></div><p><b>Environment: local</b> — main e02167f → 25acd727 (10-15/16 re-tests), local stack (not a deployed build); run folder <code>runs/2026-10-14-local</code>, lane newspec-c.</p><p><b>Test method:</b> VISUAL · Visual (screenshots for a person) — as classified in cases/test-methods.json, which says it runs on both; Source: <code>newspec-c</code>.</p><p><b>UAT item:</b> TC-06 Admission Status Toggle · <b>Section:</b> A1 · Home Screen &amp; Dashboard · <b>Scenario:</b> TC-06/S22</p><p><b>Badge control on phone widths and WebKit: tappable, not covered or clipped</b></p><p><b>Tickets:</b> TFA-92584 Admission Status Toggle (ready for qa)</p><p><b>New local lane</b> <code>newspec-c</code>: status <b>record-only</b> in <code>newspec-c/results.json</code> → <b>passed</b> (record only (every judged cell passed, the rest is recorded only)).</p><p><b>Detail:</b></p><pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">Our own addition: record-only, findings are suggestions. Same run as S21 (Pixel 7 Chromium 412 px, iPhone 15 WebKit 393 px, plus desktop). The transparent status select was measured directly (the visual lane skips opacity-0 elements): it fills its outer &lt;label&gt; exactly, 88x20 CSS px, on all four chart screens and all three profiles. 20 px is below the 24 px of WCAG 2.5.8 but passes its spacing exception (the nearest other target is 99 px from the control's centre on the Hospital chart, 33 px on the Nursing Home chart); it is below the ideal 44 pt (suggestion). The topmost element at the badge's centre is the select itself (a tap reaches it, nothing covers it); the badge text 'Follow-up ▾' is not clipped and the badge sits inside the screen on both phones; no covered / overflow / truncated finding of medium or high severity on any of the six screens. The add forms' Encounter Type control is visible without sideways scroll on both phones (page width = viewport); on Pixel 7 it is 37 px tall, on iPhone 15 WebKit 22 px tall (&lt; 24 px, WebKit's native select height), and the Note Format picker is also 22 px tall on WebKit (41 px on Chromium) - suggestions for a real-device look.</pre><p><b>Evidence:</b> 26 attached.</p><p><b>Dev run:</b> skipped: not runnable on dev — not-runnable-on-dev: visual-screens — Lane V (visual-lane.ts, local fixture).. This local result replaces that dev entry (the scenario appears once).</p>","environment":"default","setup":[],"teardown":[],"history":[],"retries":[],"breadcrumbs":[["TC-06 Admission Status Toggle","S22 Badge control on phone widths and WebKit: tappable, not covered or clipped"]],"retry":false,"titlePath":[],"retriesCount":0,"attachments":[{"link":{"used":true,"missed":false,"id":"d0f96dbdeaf5b4d352ac0100e0bddb7e","originalFileName":"cc726516-f22f-4bf9-9baf-dcc1ea6fab9c-attachment.json","ext":".json","contentType":"application/json","contentLength":4377,"name":"newspec-c/evidence/tc06-s21-s22-pixel7-hospital-add.json"},"type":"attachment"},{"link":{"used":true,"missed":false,"id":"e88b7bd7c7407632823211645da606c7","originalFileName":"de18e5c8-9579-4a09-93b9-e6dacc0d4be1-attachment.png","ext":".png","contentType":"image/png","contentLength":191469,"name":"newspec-c/evidence/tc06-s21-s22-pixel7-hospital-add.png"},"type":"attachment"},{"link":{"used":true,"missed":false,"id":"b15e7da901e14fbe0b1f88e78a5d9751","originalFileName":"850f315a-aa62-4c81-b06a-26de131fcd9b-attachment.json","ext":".json","contentType":"application/json","contentLength":2813,"name":"newspec-c/evidence/tc06-s21-s22-pixel7-hospital-chart-encounter.json"},"type":"attachment"},{"link":{"used":true,"missed":false,"id":"3fcc90a559763ecc898a5affa0ee7be3","originalFileName":"7d0c3d59-b8cf-4188-a77f-c7d79cb6e6fc-attachment.png","ext":".png","contentType":"image/png","contentLength":158329,"name":"newspec-c/evidence/tc06-s21-s22-pixel7-hospital-chart-encounter.png"},"type":"attachment"},{"link":{"used":true,"missed":false,"id":"070d273c0763429fe17976c40abd144b","originalFileName":"83e40843-bebc-4580-9d7b-9f7b1554a0f5-attachment.json","ext":".json","contentType":"application/json","contentLength":3